class=\"lex-cite-scope\">19.400</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.394</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ν. κρατεῖν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">35</span> </span>,<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">955</span> </span>, etc.: also used Adverbially with the Art., <span class=\"gk\">καὶ τὸ πάλαι</span> ( v.l. παλαιόν ) <span class=\"gk\">καὶ τὸ ν.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.26</span> </span>: in Prose <span class=\"gk\">νεωστί</span> (q.v.): rarely <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Comp.</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Adv.</span> <span class=\"gk\">νεωτέρως,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Lg.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">907c</span> </span>: <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Sup.</span> </span> <span class=\"gk\">νεώτατα</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">most recently,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Th.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.7</span> </span>; also <span class=\"gk\">ἐκ νέας,</span> <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Ion.</span> </span> <span class=\"gk\">αὖτις ἐκ νέης,</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">anew, afresh,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.60</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.116</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">IV</span>. the degrees of <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Comp.</span> </span> are <span class=\"gk\">νεώτερος, νεώτατος,</span> v. νεώτερος: <span class=\"gk\">νεαίτερος</span> is corrupt for <span class=\"gk\">νεαίρετος</span> in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">330</span> </span>. (<span class=\"gk\">νέϝος</span> (in <span class=\"gk\">νεϝόστατος,</span> q.v.), cf. Skt. <b class=\"lex-tr\">návas,</b> Lat. <b class=\"lex-tr\">novus,</b> etc.)</div></div><div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">νεός</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">νεός</span> (sc. <span class=\"gk\">γῆ</span>), <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> v. νειός. </div></div><div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">νεός</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">νεός</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Ion.</span> </span> gen. of <span class=\"gk\">ναῦς.</span></div>"}